														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4770182">
									

<p>The SCP Foundation doesn't really have a monopoly on the &quot;governmental organization that studies weird things&quot; concept. The X-Files was doing this since the 90's, Warehouse 13 a bit later, and &quot;real world&quot; inspirations include places like Area 51, the MIB (the supernatural theory that inspired the films), and so forth. It's a pretty easy way to contain disparate science fiction and horror stories into a single, contained universe. One X-Files episode would have the agents tracking down a leech monster living in the sewers, and the next would have them battling a moon ghost, and later they'd be dealing with robotic insects and alien pregnancies, in the same canon.</p>

							</div>

								
